{"text": "MEMORANDUM April 2, 1976\nTO: Dr. H. J. Minnemeyer\nFROM: M. 8. Ireland, 7. M. Larson, J. Morgan\n\nSUBJECT: Nicotine Addition\n\nA series of cigarettes were made using \"Now\" tobacco, paper\nand filters. Normal delivery is 2 mg tar and 0.2 mg nicotine.\nAn increase of 0.4 mg/cigarette was the objective. The cigarettes\nwere smoked by J. Shore, T. Jessup and H. Smith. Nicotine analysis\nwas carried out in the Nicotine Lab. Samples 1, 2 and 3 were made\nusing activated carbon, Budsweet and nicotine at 20, 40 and 80 mg/g\nrespectively. Sample #4 was sprayed with 40 mg/g nicotine and\nwater only. Sample #5 was made substituting a cheese by-product\n(Beatrice Food 80k) in place of carbon with 40 mg/g nicotine.\nSamples 6 and 8 had 40 mg/g tobacco nicotine, with #6 using nicotine,\nF\u00a2 11 and activated carbon, number 8 substituted Beatrice Food\nproduct 80 k for the carbon.\nTobacco weight in cigarettes was around 600 mg. See attached\ntable for results.\nA literature search has been completed on the physiological\neffects of nicotine.\nTt should be noted that the cigarettes were hand-made in a\nhurry, and perhaps the work should be repeated. As can be seen\nfrom the table, we were unable to increase the level more than\n0.2 mg/cigarette.\n\nXe: Dr. F. J. Schultz\n\nVEevLessy",
